  "details": "In the past the Xbox One controller barely worked with VRChat on Quest with odd behavior. I noticed the input system was updated, so I decided to try it out again. The controller has more functionality than before, but for some reason the framerate drops significantly when the view button is held. This can be recreated through the following steps:\n1. Have your Xbox One Controller connected to the Quest 2.\n2. Enter a world in VRChat.\n3. Hold the view button.\n\n(This issue appears to be fixed in [1200], the view button now only causes a single stutter when pressed.)",
